      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling for community companion animals"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients consistently report that their dogs and cats receive careful, empathetic attention throughout spay and neuter procedures. Rescue volunteers and local pet owners frequently bring in foster pets, feral colony cats, and adopted puppies, emphasizing that the veterinary team handles each animal with dedication and respect."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Dependable surgical outcomes and smooth recovery"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers emphasize smooth, uncomplicated healing following spay, neuter, and urgent soft-tissue procedures such as emergency pyometra surgery. Pet parents report that their animals recovered rapidly with minimal discomfort, noting clear discharge instructions, effective pain management, and follow-up support from the clinical staff."
      }
    }
